# Mesh and texture assets — 2.4 GB on disk. Shipped separately as
# husky_viz_models.zip rather than committed: seven files exceed GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file limit, and git cannot delta-compress binaries.
#
# The zip is the only copy of two files that are NOT in the upstream asset
# packs and cannot be recovered by re-copying them:
#   models/tree_8/bark8_collision.obj                    repaired vertex normals
#   models/terreno_lago/materials/textures/lago_textura.jpg   8192² RGB conversion
# Without the first, DART segfaults on the tree collision mesh; without the
# second, lake's terrain renders untextured. Keep the zip.
#
# For reference, 2.2 GB of the 2.4 GB is referenced by nothing — full-res
# variants superseded by _lowpoly, a Blender source file Gazebo cannot read,
# and the pre-conversion PNG texture. Verified against worlds/park.sdf and
# worlds/lake.sdf including the .mtl texture chain, 2026-08-26:
#   models/terreno_lago/lago_entero.dae                  342 MB
#   models/tree_8/uploads_files_2812146_...AcerNikoense_8.blend  308 MB
#   models/terreno_parque/terreno_parque.dae             290 MB
#   models/terreno_lago/lago.dae                         243 MB
#   models/terreno_lago/lago_1.dae                       219 MB
#   models/terreno_lago/lago_2.dae                       216 MB
#   models/terreno_lago/materials/textures/lago_textura.png      125 MB
#   models/camino_parque/camino_parque.dae                81 MB
models/

# Manual backups from editing sessions. Git supersedes these.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.bak[0-9]*

# macOS resource forks that ride along with the asset packs
._*
.DS_Store

# Credentials — never commit. This repo is public.
token.txt
*.token
.env

# Local scratch
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
